\f1\fs22 Eloise Shakti summoned Alexander to her other other office. Shakti Tower, with its wrap-around windows and Layer-filtering glass, was where she intimidated people. Her preferred workplace was her office in residence at Sublime Point. Alexander neither deserved not merited either of those. Her other other office \'97a smaller downtown suite where she did real work while in the city, unbothered by anyone worth impressing. The art adorning its walls looked suspiciously like accidents involving industrial paint supplies, yet somehow had appraised values that could sustain a small nation for several fiscal quarters. Her desk was carved from a single piece of rainforest hardwood that Eloise acquired after seventeen environmental exemptions and the sudden, mysterious retirement of three government officials.\
